  "id": "COMPOUND:22165 - PROTEIN:1146",
  "verbalization": "Multiflorin B is implicated in the biological activity of Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit through a multi-step pathway. The evidence suggests that Multiflorin B directly targets A-375, which in turn is a target of Garcihombronanes C. This chain of targets ultimately leads to the Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit. Additionally, Multiflorin B is shown to target another entity, gastric inhibitory polypeptide, which is also a target of a different compound, 2,3,4,5-Tetrabromo-6-(3,5-Dibromo-2-Hydroxyphenoxy)Phenol. While the exact mechanism linking these targets to Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit remains unclear, the integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Multiflorin B in modulating the activity of this structural subunit through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence supports a functional relationship between Multiflorin B and Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit, though the precise molecular mechanism underlying this interaction requires further investigation.",
